node_modules/
.next/
out/
.env*.local
.DS_Store

# The local junk drawer. device tooling cannot delete files, so anything
# awaiting deletion is moved here instead -- it should never be committed.
# (Four files were tracked here before this line existed. Untracked and
# deleted on 30 August 2026; the folder is gone. Keep the rule anyway --
# the next session that cannot delete a file will recreate it.)
_to_delete/

# Added automatically by `vercel link` on 30 August 2026. The CLI writes two
# rules; only one of them is kept.
#
# .vercel  -- correct, and needed. It holds the project and org ids that tie
# this working copy to the Vercel project. Machine-specific, not shared.
.vercel

# The CLI's second rule was a bare `.env*`, and it is removed deliberately.
# It is broader than it looks: it matches `.env.example`, which this project
# COMMITS on purpose as the names-only template. That file survived only
# because it was already tracked -- gitignore does not evict a tracked file --
# so the breakage would not have shown up until somebody added, say,
# `.env.production.example` and watched git silently refuse to see it.
#
# `.env*.local` on line 4 already covers the file that actually matters
# (`.env.local`, which is what `vercel env pull` writes). That is also what
# Next.js ships in its own template, for this same reason.
#
# If `.env*` reappears at the bottom of this file, a later `vercel link` put
# it back. Delete it again.

# Claude Code's per-machine permission allowlist. It records which commands
# one person has approved on one computer, with that computer's paths in it,
# so it is machine-specific in the same way `.vercel` is. It was swept into
# the Phase 1 commit by accident and untracked on 15 September 2026; the
# local file is kept, git just stops watching it. A shared `.claude/settings.json`
# (no `.local`) would be the place for rules everyone should get.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Claude Code's own working folders (28 Oct 2026): agent worktrees and the
# preview launcher. Never part of the site; GitHub Desktop listed them as changes.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/launch.json
